{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1497048936,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMzQ5NTY2OTc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1553","origin":"github"},"title":"datalad install in master uses 'url' from .gitmodules as a source of last resort??","message":"As originally appeared in #1549, datalad install -r failed on  https://github.com/psychoinformatics-de/studyforrest-data  although it works with 0.5.x version (besides the #1549 issue which is complimentary to this one I think):\nwith 0.5.x (0.5.1.dev132)\n```shell\n*yoh@hopa:/tmp\u003e datalad install -r  https://github.com/psychoinformatics-de/studyforrest-data\n[INFO   ] Installing dataset at /tmp/studyforrest-data from https://github.com/psychoinformatics-de/studyforrest-data \n[INFO   ] Installing subdataset \u003cDataset path=/tmp/studyforrest-data/aligned\u003e \n[INFO   ] Submodule HEAD got detached. Resetting branch master to point to 72b577b3. Original location was 47e53498 \n[INFO   ] Installing subdataset \u003cDataset path=/tmp/studyforrest-data/freesurfer\u003e \n[INFO   ] Installing subdataset \u003cDataset path=/tmp/studyforrest-data/multires7T\u003e \n[INFO   ] Submodule HEAD got detached. Resetting branch master to point to bad942cc. Original location was 869c290c \n[INFO   ] Installing subdataset \u003cDataset path=/tmp/studyforrest-data/phase2\u003e \n[INFO   ] Submodule HEAD got detached. Resetting branch master to point to 5cd35c44. Original location was fbb5d619 \n[INFO   ] Installing subdataset \u003cDataset path=/tmp/studyforrest-data/structural\u003e \n[INFO   ] Installing subdataset \u003cDataset path=/tmp/studyforrest-data/templatetransforms\u003e \n[INFO   ] Submodule HEAD got detached. Resetting branch master to point to 98584d15. Original location was 424d1252 \n[INFO   ] Obtaining \u003cDataset path=/tmp/studyforrest-data/aligned\u003e underneath . recursively \n[INFO   ] Installing subdataset /tmp/studyforrest-data/aligned/src/phase1 \nUsername for 'https://github.com': \n```\nand with master (0.5.1.dev543) we fail since it seems to ignore url entirely and just build candidate urls from the paths (as shown in #1549):\n```shell\nyoh@hopa:/tmp\u003e datalad install -r  https://github.com/psychoinformatics-de/studyforrest-data\n[INFO   ] Cloning dataset from 'https://github.com/psychoinformatics-de/studyforrest-data' to '/tmp/studyforrest-data' \ninstall(ok): /tmp/studyforrest-data (dataset)\n[INFO   ] Installing \u003cDataset path=/tmp/studyforrest-data\u003e recursively \n[INFO   ] Cloning dataset from 'https://github.com/psychoinformatics-de/studyforrest-data/aligned' to '/tmp/studyforrest-data/aligned' \n[ERROR  ] Failed to clone data from any candidate source URL: ['https://github.com/psychoinformatics-de/studyforrest-data/aligned', 'https://github.com/psychoinformatics-de/studyforrest-data/aligned/.git'] [install(/tmp/studyforrest-data/aligned)] \n[INFO   ] Cloning dataset from 'https://github.com/psychoinformatics-de/studyforrest-data-aligned.git' to '/tmp/studyforrest-data/aligned' \n[INFO   ] Submodule HEAD got detached. Resetting branch master to point to 72b577b3. Original location was 47e53498 \ninstall(ok): aligned (dataset) [Installed subdataset \u003cDataset path=/tmp/studyforrest-data/aligned\u003e]\n[INFO   ] Cloning dataset from 'https://github.com/psychoinformatics-de/studyforrest-data-aligned.git/src/phase1' to '/tmp/studyforrest-data/aligned/src/phase1' \n[ERROR  ] Failed to clone data from any candidate source URL: ['https://github.com/psychoinformatics-de/studyforrest-data-aligned.git/src/phase1', 'https://github.com/psychoinformatics-de/studyforrest-data-aligned.git/src/phase1/.git'] [install(/tmp/studyforrest-data/aligned/src/phase1)] \n[INFO   ] Cloning dataset from 'https://github.com/psychoinformatics-de/phase1' to '/tmp/studyforrest-data/aligned/src/phase1' \nUsername for 'https://github.com': ^CERROR: \nInterrupted by user while doing magic:  [subprocess.py:_communicate_with_poll:1152]\n\nyoh@hopa:/tmp\u003e datalad ls -r studyforrest-data/\nstudyforrest-data                      [git]  master  - 2016-03-01/06:20:45  X\nstudyforrest-data/aligned              [annex]  master  - 2016-01-20/04:43:59  X\nstudyforrest-data/aligned/src/phase1   not installed\nstudyforrest-data/aligned/src/phase2   not installed\nstudyforrest-data/aligned/src/tnt      not installed\nstudyforrest-data/freesurfer           not installed\nstudyforrest-data/multires7T           not installed\nstudyforrest-data/phase2               not installed\nstudyforrest-data/structural           not installed\nstudyforrest-data/templatetransforms   not installed\n```\n\nso it did install `aligned` from the url, but only after trying in an independent trial first to install by using paths, failing, logging an ERROR about that, and then trying a URL.  IMHO \n\n1. URL should have been tried first when provided\n2. all candidate urls should be tried in a single attempt, so we do not get those misleading ERROR messages that candidates were tried and none succeeded.","files":null}]}